course: dictionary
lesson: 5046
title: Inner: inside, and inside your head
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inner means inside, or nearer the middle of something. Look at the words next to it to find out which meaning fits. «The inner core is a solid ball of iron and nickel» tells you the core is the middle part of the Earth, so inner means inside.
explain: Inner can also describe thoughts and feelings that you keep private, which other people cannot see. «An inner critic is the mean voice in your head» means a voice that criticises you in your own mind. Nobody else hears it, so the word inner shows that it is private.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning in place of the word and read the sentence again. «The inner ear helps you hear and balance» still makes sense with inside: the inside part of your ear helps you hear and balance. If your meaning does not fit, check again.
fact: Inner means inside, or nearer the middle.
fact: Inner can describe private thoughts and feelings that you do not show, like «inner peace» or your «inner self».
fact: «The inner core» is the middle of the Earth: a solid ball of iron and nickel, about as hot as the surface of the Sun.
fact: The inner core stays solid because the enormous pressure of everything above squeezes it, even though it is very hot.
fact: The inner ear helps you hear and balance, which is why skaters rely on it.
exercise: In «The inner core is a solid ball of iron and nickel», what does inner mean? | *Inside, nearer the middle | Very cold | Made of wood | Outside, on the surface
exercise: «An inner critic is the mean voice in your head.» What does inner suggest here? | *A private voice in your own thoughts, not spoken aloud | A voice from the Sun | A loud voice you can hear from across the playground | A voice on the radio
exercise: Which word means nearer the middle? | surface | *inner | outer | edge
test: The planets Mercury, Venus, Earth and Mars are called the ... planets. | cold | outer | bright | *inner
test: «Inner peace» describes what? | A tyre for a bike | *A calm feeling inside you | A loud noise in a busy city | A round ball of metal
exam: «The inner core stays solid despite the heat because the enormous pressure of everything above squeezes it.» Why does the inner core stay solid? | It is wrapped in ice | It is cooled by the sea | It floats in water | *Huge pressure from above squeezes it
